From 7a5b95290d4e0a5fec24a0c40c77833566758def Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanidhya Awasthi <sanidhya.awasthi@bfhl.in>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:34:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Don't send a starting balance of 0 when only the starting
 date is set

Linking a bank account defaulted the custom starting balance to 0. Editing
only the starting date kept that default and sent it to the server, which
treats any defined balance as the real opening balance instead of deriving
one from the bank, so the account opened out of sync.

Leave the balance undefined until the user enters one. The amount input still
shows 0, and a balance the user deliberately sets to 0 is still sent.

Closes #8105
